          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "śuṣyati is the present of the root √śuṣ, \"to dry, wither\" (MW). MW thinks the root was first suṣ, and compares Greek auō, \"I dry\", and Lithuanian sausas, \"dry\", so it is inherited from Indo-European."
            }
          ]
        },
