              "text": "ārabhate is built on ā- and the root √rabh, \"to take hold of\" (MW), which MW connects with √labh, \"to obtain\". In the Rigveda it means \"seizes\", and from the Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa \"undertakes, begins\" (CDIAL 1305): to begin is to take hold of a task."
